  "analysis_markdown": "## 1. Search Intent Classification\n\n150 autocomplete suggestions were collected across 35 answered queries (2 of 37 queries were throttled by Google and returned nothing). The set is dominated by **destination-qualified commercial searches** — people who already know they want a villa and are narrowing by place, size and season.\n\n| Intent | Keywords | Share | Typical example |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Commercial | 68 | 45% | best luxury villa rentals in bali |\n| Transactional | 38 | 25% | luxury villa rentals for sale florida |\n| Informational | 36 | 24% | how do luxury villa rentals work |\n| Navigational | 8 | 6% | luxury villa rentals reviews |\n\n## 2. Top Topic Clusters\n\nFive clusters account for roughly three quarters of the set.\n\n- **Destination + villa (largest cluster).** Bali, Tuscany, Mykonos, Phuket and Costa Rica lead. Almost always paired with \"best\", \"private pool\" or a month.\n- **Group size and occasion.** Weddings, family reunions, bachelorette parties. \"Sleeps 12\" and \"big groups\" recur.\n- **Amenity qualifiers.** Private pool, chef included, beachfront, staffed, hot tub.\n- **Price and value.** \"Cost per night\", \"cheap options\", \"worth it\", discount codes.\n- **Process and trust.** Deposits, cancellation policy, insurance, \"vs renting a hotel\".\n\n## 3. Search Patterns Worth Noting\n\n- Modifier order is stable: *quality → type → place → amenity*. Page titles that follow that order will match more queries.\n- Question queries are almost all about **trust and mechanics**, not inspiration — deposits, insurance, cancellation.\n- The letters `q` and `x` returned nothing this run; that is a Google throttling artifact, not a sign the niche lacks those terms.\n- \"Villa\" and \"villas\" both appear at volume in adjacent research — do not consolidate them away in internal reporting.\n\n## 4. Content Opportunities\n\n- **Destination landing pages** for the leading places, each with a private-pool and sleeps-N filter visible above the fold.\n- **A plain-English \"how villa rentals work\" guide** covering deposits, cancellation and insurance.\n- **Occasion pages** for weddings and bachelorette trips, which currently have no dedicated entry point.\n- **A price and value explainer** comparing villas to hotels, targeting the \"worth it\" and \"vs renting a hotel\" queries directly.\n\n---\n\nGenerated from 150 keywords across 35 source queries · mock mode.",
